  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/63647b99-2e2d-4909-8fe1-6b3f7787dd1a-9895803_2.PNG\" style=\"width: 222px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>As electric field inside the charged conducting sphere is zero, therefore potential will be constant for the inside part.</p><p>For outside part, electric potential decreases as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and the conducting sphere behaves like a point charge concentrated at the centre.&nbsp;</p>",
